<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What the FileProvider can serve — and only once PathGuard has allowed the file, for the URI an intent
    grants. Read Files Tech is a file explorer: opening or sharing any of the user's files is its job.

    - external-path ".": the primary shared storage (/storage/emulated/0), as the 2.15.x.
    - root-path "storage/": the other volumes (/storage/XXXX-XXXX, an SD card, a USB key). The 2.15.x
      had only the line above, so a file on an SD card could neither be opened in another app nor shared
      (getUriForFile threw). FileProvider picks the LONGEST matching root, so the primary storage still
      goes out as "external".

    - cache-path "zip_shared/": ONE private folder, the entries of archives the user shares from the ZIP
      viewer (ZipShares), each extracted there for that share and purged at every start. Never a vault
      file's: the viewer offers no share when its file may not leave the app (docs D-028).

    - cache-path "scanner/capture/": the files the system's camera app writes the scanner's and the OCR's
      photos into (ACTION_IMAGE_CAPTURE, no CAMERA permission, docs D-027; CameraCapture): one empty file
      per photo asked for, its URI granted to the camera app for that photo only and revoked when it
      returns; the scanner moves the photo at once into the scan's folder, which nothing serves
      (ScanFiles), the OCR deletes it once decoded. PathGuard lets nothing of cache/ but
      zip_shared/ out: no other way out of the app reaches these files.

    - cache-path "vault_shared/": the copies of vault files the user chose to share, decrypted on demand
      (docs D-034; VaultFiles.copy with Copy.SHARE), each in a folder of its own, purged when the vault locks,
      at the panic and at every start. PathGuard refuses this folder like the others below: only
      FileLauncher.shareVaultCopy serves it, for the URI of the share asked for.

    Nothing else private is listed: not files/ (the vault, the history), not the rest of cache/
    (the vault files decrypted for the app's own viewers, cache/vault_decrypt/).
-->
<paths>
    <external-path
        name="external"
        path="." />
    <root-path
        name="volumes"
        path="storage/" />
    <cache-path
        name="zip_entries"
        path="zip_shared/" />
    <cache-path
        name="scanner_capture"
        path="scanner/capture/" />
    <cache-path
        name="vault_shared"
        path="vault_shared/" />
</paths>
